@startuml
title D-02 Site Group, Site, Vendor System, and POS Server Relationship

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "Site Group\ncustomer lookup / payment scope" as SiteGroup {
  component "Site A\nreporting + contract +\nVendor PMS mapping + POS boundary" as SiteA
  component "Site B\noptional special-case\nsecond operational Site" as SiteB
}

component "Centralized WebPay\n/s/{slug}" as WebPay
component "VendorSystem\nconfigured Vendor PMS/HCP instance" as VendorSystem
component "Adapter codebase\nreusable vendor integration" as Adapter
component "Connector instance\nruntime deployment for VendorSystem" as Connector
component "AdapterMapping\nSite to vendor object" as Mapping
component "Site POS Server\nfiscal authority for Site" as POS

WebPay --> SiteGroup : URL resolves to payment scope
SiteGroup --> SiteA : default one Site
SiteGroup --> SiteB : special case multiple Sites
SiteA --> Mapping : mapped through
SiteB --> Mapping : mapped through
Mapping --> VendorSystem : vendorSystemId
Adapter --> Connector : implemented by
Connector --> VendorSystem : connects to
Mapping --> Connector : vendorObjectType + vendorObjectRef
SiteA --> POS : resolved Site routes fiscal issuance
SiteB --> POS : each Site has its own boundary

note bottom of Mapping
HCP ParkingLotIndexCode maps through AdapterMapping.
It is not ExitPass site_id.
Runtime vendor object key:
vendorSystemId + vendorObjectType + vendorObjectRef.
end note

@enduml
